- op: discuss  # 9db8
  at: '2026-09-18T03:28:47Z'  # 9db8
  by: agent  # 9db8
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 9db8
  clock: 3  # 9db8
  nonce: 9db8  # 9db8
  message: "SATISFIED in PR #1036 (merged, origin/dev = e71fe45cbe).\n\nCLOSURE EVIDENCE (behavioral, the item's own filed repro re-run on canonical\ndev after the merge, not on the branch):\n\n    two-arm run of the real dispatcher on ~/whole_bunch_of_repos/aardvark-dns\n    (arm B = _filter_by_file_presence monkeypatched to a no-op)\n\n      before (2035bcc935):  prefilter ON 359    OFF 367    delta 8\n      after  (e71fe45cbe):  prefilter ON 367    OFF 367    delta 0\n\n    passes producing symbols only with the pre-filter OFF: NONE\n    passes with differing symbol counts between arms:      NONE\n\nThe filed instance -- the `ini` pass short-circuited on a repo whose only\nINI-family file is test/dnsmasq.conf -- no longer reproduces, and the pass now\nemits its 7 symbols (+1 file-synthesis node) with the pre-filter ON.\n\nRIGHT-REASON, not just right-number. The fix is not a widened glob: the\ndispatcher now asks the analyzer's own enumeration via the INV-hokig\nfind_files= channel for ini / cpp / objc / fortran / verilog, so the profile\ncount IS the analyzer's candidate set by construction rather than by a list\nsomeone keeps in sync. javascript took the taxonomy route (*.mts / *.cts onto\ntypescript) because get_analyzer() resolves by LANGUAGE and the js analyzer\ndeclares four, so its find_files would have made the javascript count swallow\nevery .ts file and double-count against typescript -- a second defect traded\nfor the first.\n\nTHE CLASS IS GATED, NOT THE INSTANCE. test_prefilter_candidate_set.py::\ntest_no_analyzer_reads_files_its_taxonomy_entry_cannot_see asserts that any\nin-taxonomy analyzer whose file_patterns exceed its taxonomy extensions\ndeclares find_files. It went RED naming exactly the six measured offenders\nbefore the fix and GREEN after. That is what keeps this from becoming what\nINV-hokig became -- a real cure wired to one analyzer and left.\n\nSIDE EFFECT, disclosed: profile.languages[L].files now changes for the five\nre-wired languages, because it is now the analyzer's count rather than an\nextension glob. That is the INV-hokig invariant being satisfied, not a\nregression -- the two layers are supposed to agree -- but it does move\nper-language file/LOC numbers on repos containing .conf / .h / .F03 / .vh\nfiles. Full suite: 20453 passed, 100% coverage on every changed file.\n\nNOT CLAIMED: corpus-wide behavioural measurement. One repo carries the\nbehavioural repro. The class enumeration is exact over all 118 registered\nanalyzers, and the gate makes it self-maintaining.\n\nRESIDUAL, filed nowhere because it is not a defect: 19 analyzers remain\noutside the taxonomy and are dispatched defensively every run. That costs\nwall-clock (the pre-filter is worth ~63% of analyzer time on a small repo:\n1.50s vs 4.08s) but loses nothing, because the fail-open branch is the\nrecall-preserving direction. Pre-filtering them would require per-language\nextension sets verified against real repos -- the recall-loss direction, and\nthe direction falsification cannot see."  # 9db8
